# Disable all end-of-line conversion.
#
# Git's default on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That would mean
# a file's bytes on disk differ from its bytes in the repository, which
# breaks two things here:
#
#   1. MANIFEST.csv records a SHA-256 for every artefact. With EOL
#      conversion on, a fresh clone would compute a different checksum for
#      every text file, and `--verify` would report the whole project as
#      modified when nothing had changed.
#   2. The 800+ per-round prediction CSVs would be rewritten on every
#      checkout, making them slow to stage and noisy to diff.
#
# Keeping bytes identical everywhere costs nothing — every tool in this
# project reads LF fine on Windows.
* -text
